    ],
    "by_the_end": [
      "Know your way around dumbbells, the most common machines and a barbell",
      "Lift noticeably more on your key lifts than in week 1",
      "Have a 3-day routine you can walk in and do with confidence"
    ],
    "why_this_split": "Three full-body sessions a week means you practise every movement more than once a week, which is the fastest way to learn them. Each session trains your legs, upper body and core, so missing a day never leaves a gap.",
    "how_it_works": [
      "Weeks 1 to 2: learn the key movements with just dumbbells and a bench, so you only need one area of the gym.",
      "Weeks 3 to 4: try the Smith machine, leg press and cable machines, and a light first barbell hip thrust, while your dumbbell lifts keep going up.",
      "Weeks 5 to 6: add weight to the Smith squat and barbell hip thrust you learned in weeks 3 and 4, and finish with a checkpoint.",
      "In weeks 3 and 6 you'll re-test your key lifts to see how far you've come."
    ],
    "progression_explained": "When you hit the top of the rep range on every set with good form, we'll suggest a little more weight next time. Until then, aim for one more rep than last time.",
